@prefix agp: <https://dagalog.no/ns/agentprov#> .
@prefix bl: <https://dagalog.no/ns/backlog#> .
@prefix ghissues: <https://github.com/daghovland/rdf-datalog/issues/> .
@prefix ghpull: <https://github.com/daghovland/rdf-datalog/pull/> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix session: <https://dagalog.no/ns/agentprov/session#> .

ghpull:412 a bl:PullRequest, bl:WorkItem ;
    rdfs:label "backlog: record snapshot generation timestamp in regenerate output (#380)" ;
    bl:number 412 ;
    bl:state bl:Open ;
    bl:closesIssue ghissues:380 .

session:claudeSonnet5 a prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "Claude Sonnet 5" .

session:pr412 a agp:AgentSession ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    prov:used ghissues:380 ;
    prov:startedAtTime "2026-08-07T06:45:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-08-07T07:19:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

session:pr412Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #380 (part of the dashboard epic #378) flagged that backlog-regenerate's output carried no generation timestamp at all, so nothing consuming the checked-in snapshot.ttl could tell how stale it was relative to live GitHub state. #379/PR #394 had already established a naming/typing convention for GitHub-sourced timestamps (bl:createdAt/updatedAt/closedAt: owl:DatatypeProperty, range xsd:dateTime, RFC3339 via chrono, no separate SHACL shape). This PR's main open question was the subject: those three properties all attach to an existing bl:WorkItem, but a generation timestamp is a fact about the regeneration run itself, not any one issue or crate. Reusing an arbitrary WorkItem/Crate subject would have been semantically wrong, so a new bl:Snapshot class was added with exactly one named individual, bl:CurrentSnapshot, following the same well-known-individual-in-the-bl-namespace pattern already used for bl:Open/bl:Ready/bl:Todo -- overwritten each run rather than accumulating a history, matching how the checked-in snapshot itself is a point-in-time replacement. A new pub fn add_generated_at(ds, DateTime<Utc>) was added to backlog/src/loader.rs and called from regenerate.rs's main() specifically, not from build_snapshot itself, since build_snapshot is also exercised by fixture-based tests where a live 'now' timestamp isn't meaningful recorded data -- keeping the wall-clock read at the one call site that actually needs it. The existing plain-text '# Generated by ...' header comment was kept and extended with a '# Generated at: <RFC3339>' line alongside the new queryable triple, per the issue's own suggestion that the two approaches are complementary, not exclusive. TDD: added generated_at_is_emitted to backlog/tests/loader_test.rs, confirmed it failed to compile against the old code (no add_generated_at existed) before implementing. Verified tests/serve_backlog_provenance.rs, tests/backlog_ontology.rs, tests/backlog_queries.rs, and tests/provenance_queries.rs all still pass unchanged -- the vocabulary/shapes addition introduces no closed-shape constraints that could reject the new triples." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:412 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr412 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .
